  "critical_findings": [
    "Cross-answer-model validation is positive: Sonnet as the fixed answer model still benefits materially from every UCG bundle arm.",
    "Opus semantic bundle is strongest in this run at 1.0000 task completion; Gemini bundle is 0.9859; Sonnet bundle is 0.9062; Oracle gold-admission bundle is 0.9406.",
    "The result shows that UCG bundle quality generalizes beyond a Gemini answer model; the strongest bundle in the Sonnet-answer run comes from the Opus semantic assessor, not the answer model family.",
    "The Oracle gold-admission bundle is below selective UCG bundles on downstream task completion. This does not mean UCG beats a perfect oracle; it shows that admitting all gold-allowed evidence can be less useful than selective admission when distractors/conflicts are present.",
    "Sonnet semantic admission remains the main failure seam at TU-04 because its frozen assessor produced an empty bundle. XP-04 is a secondary cross-account coverage seam.",
    "XP-03 is handled substantively by the Sonnet answer model; it exposes the authority conflict rather than fabricating a resolved decision.",
    "Absolute scores must not be compared with the earlier Gemini-answer run because the judge model changed. Within-run arm deltas and rankings are the valid comparison."
  ],
